AUDIO: 'developers with four thousand commits each, 28,000 stars on GitHub, and Software Freedom Conservancy-curated status. Entire product categories: road routers, mesh systems, and half of the'

[01:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'commercial firmware you\'ve used actually run on OpenWrt. What do you get after flashing? A writable filesystem with thousands of packages. Ad blocking at the router level for the entire network to'

[01:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'protect every device. WireGuard or OpenVPN built right at the edge of your network. Intelligent queue management that eliminates bufferbloat is the biggest real speed boost for most homes. VLAN to isolate your Smart TV'

[02:04] [scene:talk]
